OmicsLM reuses the multimodal placeholder mechanism provided by the Qwen3-VL template [Bai et al., 2025], but no visual encoder is used. Each omics profile is represented in the prompt by a single <omics> placeholder token, which is replaced by the projected omics embedding P θ ( v j ) . This lets omics profiles enter the LLM as continuous token embeddings while preserving the surrounding natural-language prompt. Formally, for text tokens x i and omics vectors v j , the input embedding sequence becomes
